<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_06_campaign_flow" name="06-campaign-flow"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1340" pageHeight="790" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="The campaign flow: predict before you measure, freeze the plan, build up in tiers, gate every window, then attribute the first limit" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1300" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="predict" value="1. PREDICT - compute-budget ledger (C1)&#10;t = FLOP/R + bytes/B + t_CPU per stage.&#10;R, B MEASURED on target, not datasheet.&#10;Name bound class + falsifiable predictions.&#10;Small batch-1 models = launch-bound." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="66" width="280" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="prereg" value="2. PRE-REGISTER (C5)&#10;Freeze hypotheses, PASS/FAIL thresholds,&#10;and the seeded run order BEFORE data.&#10;No tuning after data. Disclose anything&#10;seen early." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="360" y="66" width="280" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="solo" value="3. SOLO runs (C2)&#10;Each service alone: L1 engine / L2 deployed /&#10;L3 + upstream. DRIVE event-driven services&#10;(no idle floors). Clean baseline = the&#10;DENOMINATOR for interference." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="66" width="280" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="review1" value="4. REVIEW&#10;Independent second person checks the&#10;solo baselines, gate logic, and statistics&#10;before the combined runs begin." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1000" y="66" width="300" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="combined" value="5. COMBINED runs in TIERS (C6), seeded INTERLEAVED order (C5)&#10;Build up the stack: default load -&gt; next-generation -&gt; + manipulation -&gt; + on-demand large models.&#10;Interleave A/B (ABBA / mirror) so slow drift cancels; replicate blocks; paired within-block comparisons.&#10;Interference factor = combined value / solo sum, read per KPI (the TAIL, not the mean)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="200" width="600" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gate" value="6. VALIDITY GATES per window (C4) - warm-up then a fixed window from a sample-count rule&#10;alive (rate DROP is an outcome, silence is a void) | expected input rates | crash scan | foreign-CPU census | clocks locked at BOTH ends&#10;=&gt; each window is VALID (counts) / FLAGGED (kept with caveat) / VOID (thrown out, with a recorded void class)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="200" width="620" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="valid" value="VALID&#10;numbers count" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="336" width="195" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="flagged" value="FLAGGED&#10;kept with a caveat" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="890" y="336" width="195" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="void" value="VOID&#10;record the void class" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1100" y="336" width="200" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="carries" value="7. 'CARRIES' VERDICT per KPI band (C6), over valid windows&#10;Each timing KPI (control-loop misses, camera rate, perception rate, VLA rate) has pre-set bands:&#10;PASS band | UNRESOLVED zone | FAIL band.&#10;A cell CARRIES only if EVERY applicable KPI is PASS. Any FAIL =&gt; does not carry. Any UNRESOLVED (no FAIL) =&gt; unresolved." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="410" width="600" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="attrib" value="8. FIRST-LIMIT ATTRIBUTION (C6), pre-registered classifier&#10;CPU-pool (pool ~full + loser's drop tracks rising run-queue wait) | GPU (GPU-busy ~saturated, GPU loser, CPU flat) |&#10;memory (mem index high, CPU-only loser, no CPU saturation) | none-observed; a loss with no matching signal = UNATTRIBUTED.&#10;SATURATED-BASELINE caveat: if the lightest tier is already at the wall, the classifier reads unattributed BY CONSTRUCTION - report the saturation, do not pretend it found nothing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="410" width="620" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="loop" value="LOOP BACK ONLY for a HARNESS / INSTRUMENT bug (C5):  record a numbered ADDENDUM (defect, evidence, fix, impact on windows already run); if a recorded window was affected, SUPERSEDE it - re-run whole under the SAME seeds, keep the original, log it.  NEVER loop back to change stack behaviour: a surprise about the STACK is a FINDING, not a bug to tune away. No tuning after data (C5)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=12;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="566" width="1260" height="78" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend&#10;blue = a campaign step (predict -&gt; pre-register -&gt; solo -&gt; review -&gt; combined)&#10;amber = validity gates + the FLAGGED outcome   green = a verdict step (valid / carries / attribution)&#10;red = VOID / the saturated-baseline caveat (the honest failure modes)   purple = the addenda/supersede loop&#10;Arrows = campaign order; the only backward arrow is the harness-bug loop, never a stack-behaviour loop." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="664" width="620" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Source: C1 (predict-then-measure, compute-budget ledger, bound class, falsifiable predictions, launch-bound batch-1 models); C5 (pre-registration, no tuning after data, seeded interleaved ABBA/mirror order, replicate blocks, paired comparisons, addenda + supersedes, independent review); C2 (solo L1/L2/L3, idle floors, drivers); C4 (warm-up + fixed window, sample-count rule, validity gates alive/rates/crash/census/clocks, valid vs flagged vs void + void class); C6 (workload tiers, interference factor, PASS/UNRESOLVED/FAIL bands, first-limit attribution CPU/GPU/memory/none, saturated-baseline failure). No measured robot numbers." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="664" width="620" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="predict" target="prereg"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="prereg" target="solo"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="solo" target="review1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.9;entryY=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="review1" target="combined"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="combined" target="gate"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=0.1;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="gate" target="carries"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="carries" target="attrib"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.9;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="attrib" target="loop"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>